    "site_desc": "Agricultural fields, with corn and alfalfa rotation during growing season, and winter rye for winter cover crop. The Moore Fields property is 48 hectares and was given to the University of New Hampshire by Eugene L. Moore in 1941. Seventeen hectares in the northern portion of the property is wooded, with the most recent timber harvests in 2016. The remaining 31 hectares are actively cropped agricultural fields.",
